From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:41:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] state: FTS plan is per retry tick, made before the lock,
 never reused across attempts [daveey]

Review round 4: (1) on #106393's holder-changed branch the backoff had not elapsed, so the tick
skipped its pre-lock check and the gate planned under self._lock (the hub's case: the
supervised holder stops); (2) the pre-lock check also ran while a holder was present, where the
one-shot just defers; (3) a cached plan (5 min) outlived a successful one-shot, so a fresh
failure could be judged on a pre-damage check and the DROP free a shared page twice.

- No plan cache. The retry tick makes its plan just before taking self._lock, on every path
  that reaches the one-shot, and only when no foreign holder is present; the gate and the
  online path of that tick use it; it is discarded in `finally`.
- Inside a retry tick the gate never plans under the lock: with no tick plan (a holder left
  between the two checks) it skips the DROP and the next tick plans first.
- With a holder present, the online path plans for itself after the lock is released.
- The 6 h refusal memo stays.

Tests: holder leaving mid-backoff plans once, outside the lock, and the tick plan is discarded;
the gate never plans under the lock inside a tick.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
